1
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,800
It's him.

2
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:27,960
Boss.

3
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,510
I'm telling you, it's all taken care of.

4
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:30,870
Those leading companies in the province

5
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:32,200
have all agreed to back us.

6
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:35,150
Chao.

7
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:38,110
I trust you to get things done.

8
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,070
Thank you, Boss.

9
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,150
Once today's
Investment Conference is over,

10
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:43,320
we'll have plenty of money.

11
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:48,790
Boss, what about the share we agreed on?

12
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,000
What's the rush?

13
00:00:51,470 --> 00:00:53,070
If I get my share, you'll get yours.

14
00:00:54,030 --> 00:00:55,280
No talk about money today.

15
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:56,790
Just enjoy yourself.

16
00:00:58,920 --> 00:00:59,710
Thank you, Boss.

17
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,200
Such a big appetite.

18
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,040
Aren't you afraid
it'll be the death of you?

19
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:11,620
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 9=

20
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:18,760
Is this guy stupid or what?

21
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:20,510
He was knocked unconscious,
but instead of running,

22
00:01:20,710 --> 00:01:22,150
he hid inside this box.

23
00:01:22,710 --> 00:01:24,280
Then someone locked it from the outside.

24
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:26,480
A metal box this big was sitting here,

25
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:28,120
and the body became mummified,

26
00:01:28,310 --> 00:01:30,350
yet not a single passerby noticed it.

27
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,070
What's wrong, Li?

28
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:49,740
(High Voltage Danger)

29
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,760
High Voltage Danger.

30
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:53,790
Keep Away.

31
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:55,760
But the walls of the box
are covered with charcoal.

32
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,950
This isn't
a high-voltage electrical box.

33
00:01:59,510 --> 00:02:00,560
I get it.

34
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:02,480
The killer wrote those words.

35
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:04,680
He disguised it
as a high-voltage electrical box

36
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,280
and deliberately placed it
next to a utility pole.

37
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,840
When nearby residents saw

38
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,030
"High Voltage" written on the box,

39
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:15,360
they wouldn't pay attention
to it or go near it.

40
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,630
The box has double-layered metal walls

41
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:17,590
and is tightly sealed.

42
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:19,310
It has a fire-resistant coating inside.

43
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:21,030
This is a professional
charcoal storage box.

44
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:23,280
Ma, look into

45
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,910
whether anyone nearby
is in the charcoal business,

46
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:26,810
especially anyone
who shut down their business

47
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:28,030
or switched trades
between last year and this year.

48
00:02:28,030 --> 00:02:29,840
Also talk to the nearby residents

49
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:32,430
and see if anyone noticed this box

50
00:02:32,870 --> 00:02:34,470
or knows of anything unusual.

51
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:35,520
Yes.

52
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,710
Qin, calling Qin.

53
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,400
Copy.

54
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:08,280
Qin, I found something here.

55
00:03:08,910 --> 00:03:10,120
I found something here too.

56
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:12,710
You're my elder, so you go first.

57
00:03:13,310 --> 00:03:14,120
All right.

58
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,650
The autopsy report is out.

59
00:03:16,650 --> 00:03:18,120
The victim suffered a hammer
blow to the back of the head,

60
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:18,960
but it wasn't fatal.

61
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,360
The actual cause of death

62
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,150
was asphyxia.

63
00:03:21,150 --> 00:03:23,800
But because the body
is severely mummified,

64
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,960
we can't definitively find

65
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,680
any external signs of asphyxia.

66
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:28,680
The victim is Liang Chao.

67
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,150
I used technology
to reconstruct his appearance.

68
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:35,000
Liang Chao?

69
00:03:35,310 --> 00:03:36,080
Are you sure it's Liang Chao?

70
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:37,310
If it really is Liang Chao,

71
00:03:37,310 --> 00:03:39,280
he's a major suspect in Jin Juan's case.

72
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,710
What if he died three months ago?

73
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:43,800
Then we need to determine
his true cause of death.

74
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:44,630
Qin.

75
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:46,150
Did the autopsy report reveal anything?

76
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,190
The autopsy report,

77
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:49,310
and the color of the nail beds

78
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:50,590
is darker than the surrounding tissue.

79
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:56,000
The eyeballs have shriveled,
and the conjunctiva is discolored.

80
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,310
No hemorrhagic spots are visible.

81
00:03:57,750 --> 00:03:59,430
There are signs of asphyxia,
but the cause can't be found.

82
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,000
But one thing is certain.

83
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,910
He wasn't asphyxiated by compression
of the mouth and nose, neck,

84
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:05,560
or chest and abdomen.

85
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:07,240
That's right.

86
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,750
The metal box wasn't completely sealed.

87
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,190
He couldn't have suffocated inside it.

88
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,630
But what exactly happened?

89
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:15,400
How did he asphyxiate?

90
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:17,480
We found no possible
cause of death on the body's surface.

91
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:20,040
As for the internal organs,
the tissue cells had dried out,

92
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,830
so histopathological examination
couldn't be performed.

93
00:04:22,310 --> 00:04:25,070
Could his airway have been blocked?

94
00:04:26,750 --> 00:04:28,870
No foreign objects were found
in the trachea or bronchi.

95
00:04:28,870 --> 00:04:31,190
There was also no darkening in color

96
00:04:31,190 --> 00:04:32,480
from congestion or blood stasis.

97
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:33,830
There were no abnormalities
in the lungs either.

98
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:37,210
There was hemorrhaging

99
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:38,410
in the petrous parts
of both temporal bones.

100
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:41,560
But we still can't find
the cause of asphyxia.

101
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:44,920
Could it be...

102
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,920
The bronchioles?

103
00:05:05,950 --> 00:05:06,750
Qin.

104
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,480
There really is something
in the bronchioles.

105
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,950
We found the cause
of his death by asphyxia.

106
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,070
This foreign object

107
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:14,920
blocked his peripheral airways.

108
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:19,800
How did you know
we'd find something there?

109
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:20,510
Intuition.

110
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:22,160
It's simple.

111
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,870
I think it's simple.

112
00:05:23,870 --> 00:05:24,560
What intuition?

113
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:25,800
You... You must have

114
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:28,190
an expert secretly coaching you.

115
00:05:28,190 --> 00:05:30,000
You can't secretly study
and get better without telling us.

116
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,720
Come on. I have
more cases than I can solve.

117
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,800
When would I have time to study, right?

118
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:34,830
Right.

119
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,560
Your top priority

120
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,460
is to examine the foreign object

121
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:39,310
in the bronchioles

122
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:40,870
and find out exactly what it is.

123
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:41,480
All right?

124
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,720
Report back to me when you get back.

125
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:44,040
- Okay, Captain Qin.
- Go.

126
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,680
Whatever you say.

127
00:05:46,190 --> 00:05:47,000
Go.

128
00:05:50,716 --> 00:05:51,806
That rascal.

129
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,360
He's really something.

130
00:05:57,390 --> 00:05:58,190
Qin.

131
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:03,800
The foreign object
test results are back.

132
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:06,070
They're tissue fibers.

133
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,920
You mean ordinary toilet paper?

134
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,310
It's ordinary toilet paper,

135
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:12,160
but it's also a little different.

136
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:12,750
No. Just tell me.

137
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:14,040
Is it ordinary or not?

138
00:06:14,390 --> 00:06:15,070
Then it's not ordinary.

139
00:06:15,070 --> 00:06:15,720
So it's special.

140
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:16,270
Special.

141
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:17,920
Because its fiber structure
is unusually dense.

142
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:19,190
Special is good.
That makes it easier to find.

143
00:06:19,270 --> 00:06:20,040
That's a good thing.

144
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,600
That's what I'm telling you.
It's good news.

145
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,920
Enough nonsense.

146
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,680
Actually, there's something else.

147
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:25,560
I want to ask you something.

148
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,190
Ask.

149
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:27,680
Forget it. I won't ask.

150
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,160
What's with you?

151
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:30,950
You can't just stop halfway through.

152
00:06:31,510 --> 00:06:32,360
Spit it out.

153
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:34,070
All right, then let me ask you.

154
00:06:34,430 --> 00:06:36,800
With our current
facial reconstruction technology,

155
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:39,040
I don't think we can identify
a person with certainty.

156
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,390
So how did you know it was Liang Chao?

157
00:06:45,830 --> 00:06:47,000
I knew you wouldn't be able to hold back

158
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,160
from asking me that.

159
00:06:50,190 --> 00:06:51,310
Let me put it this way.

160
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:52,680
Actually,

161
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,950
I have a partner

162
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:58,000
in the future.

163
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:00,390
You know?

164
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,390
He's my son.

165
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:04,510
He's a great
medical examiner in the future.

166
00:07:04,510 --> 00:07:07,120
Qin, that's not funny.

167
00:07:07,310 --> 00:07:09,480
If you don't want
to tell me, then don't.

168
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,040
What, do you think I'm a three-year-old?

169
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,040
You think I'm that easy to fool?

170
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:13,190
I just like fooling you.

171
00:07:13,270 --> 00:07:14,630
I like picking on you.

172
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:15,560
What are you going to do about it?

173
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,310
Go deal with the tissue paper. Hurry.

174
00:07:17,510 --> 00:07:20,040
Fine, Captain Qin. You're the boss.

175
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:25,480
You want me to go to the supermarket
and take every kind of tissue paper

176
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,600
to the Forensic Science Institute?

177
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,120
But Captain Qin,

178
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:29,070
I still have paperwork to do.

179
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:30,950
Just go. Enough nonsense.

180
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,950
We have a new lead. That's a good thing.

181
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:33,720
Hurry.

182
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:34,720
Yes.

183
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:35,750
Come on, you...

184
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:36,430
Qin.

185
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:37,120
Chief.

186
00:07:37,630 --> 00:07:39,360
That mummified body is Liang Chao?

187
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,270
Yes.

188
00:07:40,270 --> 00:07:42,360
We always thought
he'd killed someone and fled.

189
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,560
But based on the current timeline,

190
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:47,430
he may very well
have been the first victim.

191
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:49,680
Right. The autopsies show that

192
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,190
Liang Chao, Huo Qicheng,

193
00:07:51,270 --> 00:07:53,070
and the white dog from Jin Juan's case

194
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:54,600
all suffered hammer blows to the head.

195
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,070
These aren't isolated cases.

196
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:57,830
This is a serial murder case.

197
00:07:58,040 --> 00:08:00,000
We're dealing with a brutal,

198
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,190
highly intelligent criminal.

199
00:08:01,190 --> 00:08:02,750
Captain Qin, we have a lead.

200
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,160
Chief Zhao.

201
00:08:04,390 --> 00:08:05,750
Following Captain Qin's instructions,

202
00:08:05,750 --> 00:08:07,040
I checked the demolition area.

203
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,270
There was only one person named Bai Wen

204
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:09,830
who used to sell charcoal wholesale.

205
00:08:09,830 --> 00:08:10,920
But early last year,

206
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,070
his business went under,

207
00:08:12,070 --> 00:08:13,190
and he went to Shanghai for work.

208
00:08:13,190 --> 00:08:14,190
A little over a month ago,

209
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:15,480
his family home was demolished,

210
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:16,160
so he came back.

211
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,560
He's currently staying at a hostel.

212
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,270
He came back a month ago.

213
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:22,190
But Liang Chao died three months ago.

214
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:23,800
If he'd been in Shanghai the whole time,

215
00:08:24,630 --> 00:08:25,750
he couldn't have committed the crime.

216
00:08:25,750 --> 00:08:28,480
We can't rule out the possibility
that he came back secretly.

217
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:30,240
Besides, he was
the original owner of the box.

218
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:32,030
He can tell us where the box
came from and where it went.

219
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:33,870
Most importantly, I've brought him in.

220
00:08:33,870 --> 00:08:34,670
Let's talk to him.

221
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,200
Then let's go.

222
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,200
Yes.

223
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,510
Chief Zhao.

224
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,550
You're Bai Wen, right?

225
00:08:55,630 --> 00:08:56,480
Don't be nervous.

226
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:57,720
We just want to ask you a few questions.

227
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,320
Officer.

228
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:03,150
I haven't done anything wrong, have I?

229
00:09:03,870 --> 00:09:07,120
I heard you used
to be in the charcoal business.

230
00:09:08,270 --> 00:09:11,120
What kind
of storage equipment did you use?

231
00:09:11,870 --> 00:09:13,120
Take a look. Is this it?

232
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:18,000
Yes, that's it.

233
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:20,870
I had Liu's Blacksmith Shop
in the south of the city

234
00:09:20,870 --> 00:09:22,600
custom-make three of them.

235
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:23,750
Look here.

236
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:26,750
This dent was from
when we accidentally bumped it

237
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:28,000
while transporting it.

238
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,480
I remember it clearly.

239
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:34,390
What happened to these boxes afterward?

240
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:38,510
I sold two of them
to others in the same business.

241
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:41,480
I didn't have time
to move the other one,

242
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,600
so I left it at my old house.

243
00:09:43,670 --> 00:09:44,720
Your old house?

244
00:09:45,150 --> 00:09:46,360
Where exactly?

245
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:49,840
In the warehouse
where I used to store raw materials.

246
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:53,120
I kept quite
a few other things in there too.

247
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:56,080
I like trying my hand
at small businesses,

248
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:58,750
but none of them ever worked out.

249
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,200
When you left,

250
00:10:03,270 --> 00:10:05,030
did you leave the key with anyone,

251
00:10:05,030 --> 00:10:05,840
or

252
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:09,030
could anyone else get into your house?

253
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:10,630
I only had one set of keys.

254
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:11,670
I took them with me.

255
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:15,750
But to be honest,
the warehouse wasn't very secure.

256
00:10:15,790 --> 00:10:17,320
When I was about to leave,

257
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:19,320
a few people from my hometown heard
I was leaving

258
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:21,910
and said they wanted to go in
and look for something useful.

259
00:10:21,910 --> 00:10:22,790
I wasn't there,

260
00:10:22,790 --> 00:10:24,390
so I just let them go in themselves.

261
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:26,790
What's the situation?

262
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:28,670
Captain Qin, judging by the timeline,

263
00:10:28,670 --> 00:10:30,240
Bai Wen couldn't
have committed the crime.

264
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,360
There's clear evidence

265
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:32,510
that he did go to Shanghai,

266
00:10:32,510 --> 00:10:34,840
and he returned
after the crime occurred.

267
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,840
But Bai Wen
was the original owner of the box.

268
00:10:37,080 --> 00:10:38,440
That's very important.

269
00:10:38,750 --> 00:10:40,200
For the killer to get hold of the box,

270
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,270
he either knew Bai Wen

271
00:10:41,270 --> 00:10:42,670
or knew the old house well.

272
00:10:43,390 --> 00:10:44,550
Bai Wen said a few people
from his hometown

273
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:45,360
went there looking for things.

274
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,790
Could that be a lead?

275
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:48,910
Bai Wen did say

276
00:10:48,910 --> 00:10:50,360
the house wasn't very secure.

277
00:10:50,510 --> 00:10:52,720
The killer may not
have needed a key to get in.

278
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:55,240
Here's what we'll do.
We'll examine the scene again.

279
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:56,150
Focus on two things.

280
00:10:56,150 --> 00:10:56,630
First,

281
00:10:56,630 --> 00:10:57,960
where the box was originally placed.

282
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:58,670
Second,

283
00:10:58,670 --> 00:11:00,960
check whether there are any signs
that someone broke into the old house.

284
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:04,000
Bai Wen may not be a suspect,

285
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,750
but he's an important witness.

286
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,750
We need to keep him safe.

287
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,080
Also, look into

288
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:09,960
who those people from his hometown were.

289
00:11:10,510 --> 00:11:11,840
I have another thought.

290
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,720
I don't think the killer chose this box

291
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:15,480
by chance.

292
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:16,840
The charcoal box is very well sealed.

293
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,550
It can quickly dehydrate
and dry out a body

294
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,960
and contain the odor.

295
00:11:21,910 --> 00:11:24,270
The killer must have
had some specialized knowledge

296
00:11:25,550 --> 00:11:27,630
or may have worked
in the charcoal business.

297
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:28,840
You mean

298
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,000
the killer may have worked
in the industry before

299
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:33,360
or at least knew
something about charcoal.

300
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:36,360
So when you investigate
Bai Wen's social connections,

301
00:11:36,600 --> 00:11:38,840
make sure you look
into his peers, customers,

302
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
and suppliers.

303
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,440
Go. Be careful.

304
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:43,600
No.

305
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:54,000
Stop!

306
00:11:54,390 --> 00:11:55,200
What are you doing?

307
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,480
Get down!

308
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:59,360
We haven't even agreed on a price yet.

309
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:00,720
(Demolish)
I haven't moved my equipment out yet.

310
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,240
You smash your way in there,
are you going to pay for it?

311
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:03,960
Who are you? Get lost!

312
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,880
I'm going.

313
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:15,600
Ma.

314
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:18,200
Take some people and search the area.

315
00:12:18,790 --> 00:12:20,080
The rest of you, come with me.

316
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,030
Open the door.

317
00:12:30,030 --> 00:12:30,840
Careful.

318
00:12:31,670 --> 00:12:32,480
There are footprints.

319
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:36,670
Where was the box?

320
00:12:36,870 --> 00:12:38,360
It was originally over there.

321
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,000
Okay.

322
00:13:03,510 --> 00:13:04,600
Is this blood?

323
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:05,360
Looks like it.

324
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,270
Look.

325
00:13:06,670 --> 00:13:08,550
It's in a spatter pattern.

326
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:10,960
Zhou.

327
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:13,670
Can you tell
whether it's human or animal?

328
00:13:13,670 --> 00:13:14,270
Yes.

329
00:13:14,270 --> 00:13:15,600
We'll do a presumptive
blood test back at the lab,

330
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,840
then a species identification test.

331
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:18,120
Impressive.

332
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,750
Is this bottle yours?

333
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:32,630
No.

334
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:33,790
Officer.

335
00:13:33,790 --> 00:13:35,720
I'm allergic to alcohol. I don't drink.

336
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:38,630
Someone else
must have come here after I left.

337
00:13:41,790 --> 00:13:43,720
Someone lived here for a while.

338
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,440
This tissue paper packaging

339
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:51,030
is from a local supermarket's own brand.

340
00:13:51,030 --> 00:13:52,270
It's a niche brand.

341
00:13:53,390 --> 00:13:55,510
(Tissue Paper)
The foreign object I found inside the body

342
00:13:55,750 --> 00:13:57,270
was tissue paper fibers.

343
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,440
Take this back and compare them.

344
00:13:59,550 --> 00:14:00,750
If they match,

345
00:14:00,750 --> 00:14:01,840
and the blood matches too,

346
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:04,200
this is very likely
the primary crime scene.

347
00:14:19,390 --> 00:14:21,670
Have you lost your mind?

348
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:23,150
Let me go right now!

349
00:14:24,510 --> 00:14:25,630
Let you go?

350
00:14:27,510 --> 00:14:30,870
My family put all our hard-earned money,

351
00:14:31,480 --> 00:14:32,630
our life savings,

352
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,670
into that

353
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,390
bottomless pit of yours.

354
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:43,960
Now I have just one question.

355
00:14:44,510 --> 00:14:47,200
Back then,

356
00:14:47,790 --> 00:14:50,790
did you ever once think

357
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,480
about letting me go?

358
00:14:54,550 --> 00:14:55,360
You were greedy.

359
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:56,790
Who else can you blame?

360
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,240
Investments carry risks.

361
00:14:58,630 --> 00:14:59,790
Don't you understand that?

362
00:15:01,390 --> 00:15:04,000
Greedy poor people
should accept their fate.

363
00:15:04,150 --> 00:15:04,960
Greedy?

364
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:08,270
Who's greedier than you?

365
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:10,120
You bloodsuckers.

366
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,440
None of you will get away.

367
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:14,910
By the way,

368
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:17,030
I forgot to tell you.

369
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:18,510
Your punishment

370
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:22,120
starts tonight.

371
00:15:31,510 --> 00:15:32,320
Punishment?

372
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,200
You think you can scare me?

373
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,080
A loser like you

374
00:15:38,870 --> 00:15:40,440
thinks you can take revenge?

375
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,910
Let me go right now!

376
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,790
Let me go!

377
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,240
I forgot to tell you.

378
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:49,790
Your wife's body

379
00:15:50,270 --> 00:15:51,080
was so soft.

380
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,440
So soft.

381
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,870
You're the first.

382
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,440
Huo Qicheng.

383
00:16:03,550 --> 00:16:04,360
Jin Juan.

384
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:07,960
All you bloodsuckers

385
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:09,720
who feed off other people,

386
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,480
I'll settle the score with you

387
00:16:13,510 --> 00:16:15,670
one by one.

388
00:16:17,630 --> 00:16:19,030
And from your bodies,

389
00:16:19,030 --> 00:16:21,750
drop by drop,

390
00:16:21,750 --> 00:16:23,870
I'll drain all that blood out.

391
00:16:27,150 --> 00:16:27,960
Liars.

392
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:30,030
You're all liars.

393
00:16:41,320 --> 00:16:42,120
What are you doing?

394
00:16:44,030 --> 00:16:44,840
You can't.

395
00:16:44,910 --> 00:16:46,270
You can't die that easily.

396
00:16:47,870 --> 00:16:48,510
Swallow it.

397
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,240
Swallow it all.

398
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:51,240
Swallow it all.

399
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,360
You can't die that easily on me.

400
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,150
You hear me?

401
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:55,440
Swallow it.

402
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,240
I said swallow it.

403
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,630
I said swallow it.

404
00:16:59,630 --> 00:17:00,390
Swallow it!

405
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:40,600
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

406
00:17:43,670 --> 00:17:48,450
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

407
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:56,540
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

408
00:17:57,070 --> 00:18:02,400
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

409
00:18:04,430 --> 00:18:12,390
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

410
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:18,070
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

411
00:18:20,110 --> 00:18:28,420
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

412
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:34,270
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

413
00:18:35,730 --> 00:18:43,850
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

414
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:49,580
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

415
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:59,400
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

416
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:06,950
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

417
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:11,560
♪Can you hear me?♪

418
00:19:11,570 --> 00:19:15,360
♪Can you hear me?♪

419
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:22,820
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

420
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:30,560
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

421
00:19:30,890 --> 00:19:36,500
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

422
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:41,980
♪After all these years♪

423
00:19:44,490 --> 00:19:51,970
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

424
00:19:52,870 --> 00:19:54,170
♪And tell you♪

425
00:19:55,390 --> 00:19:58,660
♪I haven't let you down♪
